// This implies we need to re-evaluate the integral contribution if the total torque is saturated.
// However, the prompt says "recompute that axis from the previous integral".
// This is tricky. Usually, anti-windup freezes integral increment if output is saturated.
// Here it says: if axis is saturated, and the NEW integral term would make it MORE saturated, freeze.
